# mcp__basic_memory_write_note — basic-memory/write_note

Create a markdown note. If the note already exists, returns an error by default — pass overwrite=True to replace.

## Schema
```ts
type Args = {
  /** The title of the note */
  title: string;
  /** Markdown content for the note, can include observations and relations */
  content: string;
  /**
   * Directory path relative to project root where the file should be saved.
   *        Use forward slashes (/) as separators. Use "/" or "" to write to project root.
   *        Examples: "notes", "projects/2025", "research/ml", "/" (root)
   */
  directory: string;
  /**
   * Project name to write to. Optional - server will resolve using the
   *     hierarchy above. Use "workspace/project" to route to a project in a
   *     specific cloud workspace. A bare name that exists in multiple
   *     workspaces resolves to the default workspace, so use the qualified
   *     form (or project_id) to disambiguate. If unknown, use
   *     list_memory_projects() to discover available projects and their
   *     qualified names.
   */
  project?: string | null;
  /**
   * Workspace slug, name, or tenant_id. When provided with `project`,
   *     routes as `workspace/project`. Cannot be combined with `project_id`.
   */
  workspace?: string | null;
  /**
   * Project external_id (UUID). Prefer this over `project` when known —
   *     it routes to the exact project regardless of name collisions across cloud
   *     workspaces. Takes precedence over `project`. Get from list_memory_projects().
   */
  project_id?: string | null;
  /**
   * Tags to categorize the note. Can be a list of strings, a comma-separated string, or None.
   *   Note: If passing from external MCP clients, use a string format (e.g. "tag1,tag2,tag3")
   */
  tags?: string[] | string | null;
  /**
   * Type of note to create (stored in frontmatter). Defaults to "note".
   *        Can be "guide", "report", "config", "person", etc.
   */
  note_type?: string;
  /**
   * Optional dict of extra frontmatter fields merged into entity_metadata.
   *       Useful for schema notes or any note that needs custom YAML frontmatter
   *       beyond title/type/tags. Nested dicts are supported.
   */
  metadata?: Record<string, unknown> | null;
  /**
   * If True, replace existing note on conflict. If False, error on conflict.
   *        If None (default), consult write_note_overwrite_default config setting.
   */
  overwrite?: boolean | null;
  /**
   * "text" returns the existing markdown summary. "json" returns
   *            machine-readable metadata.
   */
  output_format?: "text" | "json";
};
```
Execute by writing JSON to xd://mcp__basic_memory_write_note.
Example: write(path="xd://mcp__basic_memory_write_note", content="{\"title\":\"...\"}") — one JSON object, newlines inside strings as \n.
